WEBVTT

1
00:00:28.666 --> 00:00:32.416
In the first three verses of Chapter 16,

2
00:00:32.416 --> 00:00:33.208
Lord Krishna

3
00:00:33.208 --> 00:00:36.416
described twenty-six divine qualities.

4
00:00:36.416 --> 00:00:39.791
Now He begins to describe the qualities

5
00:00:39.791 --> 00:00:42.291
of the opposite nature.

6
00:00:42.291 --> 00:00:46.500
The asuri sampat, the qualities
of the demoniac nature.

7
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:49.291
These are not merely ordinary weaknesses.

8
00:00:49.291 --> 00:00:50.625
They are deep-rooted

9
00:00:50.625 --> 00:00:54.250
tendencies and inclinations

10
00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:56.166
that keep the soul bound in ignorance,

11
00:00:56.166 --> 00:01:00.375
suffering, and the cycle of birth and death.

12
00:01:00.375 --> 00:01:02.333
In this fourth verse Lord Krishna

13
00:01:02.333 --> 00:01:05.083
briefly mentions these six principal

14
00:01:05.083 --> 00:01:07.541
negative qualities.

15
00:01:07.541 --> 00:01:10.291
From verses 16.7 to 16.20,

16
00:01:10.291 --> 00:01:12.958
He will explain them in detail.

17
00:01:17.583 --> 00:01:19.416
The six negative qualities

18
00:01:19.416 --> 00:01:22.000
described in the fourth verse are –

19
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.000
Dambhah – hypocrisy or pretence.

20
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.166
This occurs when a person displays virtues

21
00:01:29.166 --> 00:01:31.583
or spirituality

22
00:01:31.583 --> 00:01:34.625
that do not actually exist within them.

23
00:01:34.625 --> 00:01:36.250
They perform religious conduct

24
00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:38.500
or speech for show,

25
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:40.625
but their aim is only to gain praise

26
00:01:40.625 --> 00:01:42.833
and respect.

27
00:01:42.833 --> 00:01:43.625
There is a gap

28
00:01:43.625 --> 00:01:46.875
between the outer appearance
and the inner feeling.

29
00:01:46.875 --> 00:01:52.166
As if goodness is being performed,
but not truly felt.

30
00:01:52.166 --> 00:01:53.083
Darpah

31
00:01:53.083 --> 00:01:56.416
means arrogance or pride.

32
00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:58.458
Darpa arises

33
00:01:58.458 --> 00:02:00.875
when someone receives something
like intelligence,

34
00:02:00.875 --> 00:02:03.958
power, beauty, or wealth,

35
00:02:03.958 --> 00:02:04.500
and

36
00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:08.625
becomes inflated, beginning to
look down on others.

37
00:02:08.625 --> 00:02:12.041
Such a person overestimates themselves

38
00:02:12.041 --> 00:02:14.000
and those they regard as lesser,

39
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:18.041
they do not even consider it proper to look at.

40
00:02:18.041 --> 00:02:22.041
Abhimanah – hunger for respect.

41
00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:23.000
This is the inner

42
00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:26.000
thirst that constantly wants

43
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.625
people to appreciate us,

44
00:02:28.625 --> 00:02:30.708
even if no one says anything.

45
00:02:30.708 --> 00:02:32.791
The mind expects

46
00:02:32.791 --> 00:02:34.958
to be valued.

47
00:02:34.958 --> 00:02:38.625
Abhimana shows itself when,
on not receiving recognition,

48
00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:42.458
a person becomes hurt or angry.

49
00:02:42.458 --> 00:02:47.083
It arises from a false sense of ego and identity.

50
00:02:47.083 --> 00:02:50.625
Krodhah – anger.

51
00:02:50.625 --> 00:02:53.875
When desires are not fulfilled, repeated

52
00:02:53.875 --> 00:02:55.666
and uncontrolled

53
00:02:55.666 --> 00:02:59.541
anger rising is a sign of demoniac nature.

54
00:02:59.541 --> 00:03:02.041
This is not a momentary reaction,

55
00:03:02.041 --> 00:03:04.375
but becomes a character trait.

56
00:03:04.375 --> 00:03:07.208
Such a person justifies their anger

57
00:03:07.208 --> 00:03:09.666
and believes that showing outrage

58
00:03:09.666 --> 00:03:12.916
is their right.

59
00:03:12.916 --> 00:03:14.041
Parushyam

60
00:03:14.041 --> 00:03:17.916
means harsh speech and behaviour.

61
00:03:17.916 --> 00:03:19.708
This shows itself

62
00:03:19.708 --> 00:03:23.250
when anger comes out as bitter words.

63
00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:27.208
Sarcasm, mockery, insult, or saying
‘I am speaking the truth’

64
00:03:27.208 --> 00:03:29.375
and wounding

65
00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:32.166
someone is a sign of harshness and insensitivity.

66
00:03:32.166 --> 00:03:32.791
Even if

67
00:03:32.791 --> 00:03:33.916
you are right,

68
00:03:33.916 --> 00:03:36.833
harsh speech proves you wrong.

69
00:03:36.833 --> 00:03:38.833
It breaks relationships

70
00:03:38.833 --> 00:03:42.166
and destroys compassion.

71
00:03:42.166 --> 00:03:46.541
Ajnanam – spiritual ignorance.

72
00:03:46.541 --> 00:03:47.500
Ignorance

73
00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:51.000
is not merely the absence of bookish knowledge.

74
00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.666
It is the inability to distinguish between
right and wrong,

75
00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:57.166
elevation and downfall.

76
00:03:57.166 --> 00:03:58.791
Such a person, even if

77
00:03:58.791 --> 00:04:01.125
they appear clever in worldly matters,

78
00:04:01.125 --> 00:04:03.000
remains unaware of their true nature,

79
00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:06.500
their purpose, and their dharma.

80
00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:09.458
These qualities are not merely
ordinary mistakes,

81
00:04:09.458 --> 00:04:13.083
but deep tendencies arising from
the influence of Rajo Guna

82
00:04:13.083 --> 00:04:16.833
and Tamo Guna.

83
00:04:16.833 --> 00:04:20.208
If left unchecked, they gradually

84
00:04:20.208 --> 00:04:22.208
take the soul further

85
00:04:22.208 --> 00:04:25.666
and further from its spiritual path.

86
00:04:25.666 --> 00:04:28.500
Yet a person is not helpless.

87
00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:29.500
These tendencies,

88
00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:32.083
even if they have arisen from past sanskaras

89
00:04:32.083 --> 00:04:35.583
and karma, can be changed through awareness,

90
00:04:35.583 --> 00:04:36.458
practice,

91
00:04:36.458 --> 00:04:37.708
and good company.

92
00:04:37.708 --> 00:04:40.125
They can be changed.

93
00:04:40.125 --> 00:04:44.458
The choice to adopt the divine
nature is still possible today.

94
00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:49.916
When you

95
00:04:49.916 --> 00:04:53.208
only to please others, or

96
00:04:53.208 --> 00:04:54.625
to look good,

97
00:04:54.625 --> 00:04:57.166
pretend to become

98
00:04:57.166 --> 00:05:00.208
what you are not, then

99
00:05:00.208 --> 00:05:04.916
perhaps for some time people
may be confused,

100
00:05:04.916 --> 00:05:07.041
but this pretence

101
00:05:07.041 --> 00:05:11.291
stops your own growth.

102
00:05:11.291 --> 00:05:13.625
I have called this

103
00:05:13.625 --> 00:05:15.833
dambha.

104
00:05:15.833 --> 00:05:17.333
Hypocrisy.

105
00:05:17.333 --> 00:05:20.000
It is among those qualities that

106
00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:24.666
take you further from the truth.

107
00:05:24.666 --> 00:05:28.000
When you hide your weaknesses,

108
00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.083
or without sincerity only wear

109
00:05:30.083 --> 00:05:33.916
the mask of spirituality,

110
00:05:33.916 --> 00:05:38.333
you close your own path.

111
00:05:38.333 --> 00:05:41.833
Then you stop asking for help.

112
00:05:41.833 --> 00:05:44.958
You stop being honest with yourself.

113
00:05:44.958 --> 00:05:46.041
Slowly

114
00:05:46.041 --> 00:05:46.708
you begin

115
00:05:46.708 --> 00:05:49.125
to believe in the very role

116
00:05:49.125 --> 00:05:51.916
you are performing,

117
00:05:51.916 --> 00:05:55.958
and this way you drift away from becoming

118
00:05:55.958 --> 00:05:59.000
what you were meant to become.

119
00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:03.250
If someone, not being virtuous, only

120
00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:08.708
considers being wealthy as being prestigious,

121
00:06:08.708 --> 00:06:11.875
then they become entangled in appearances.

122
00:06:11.875 --> 00:06:12.750
Far more valuable than cars,

123
00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:16.166
mansions, and property

124
00:06:16.166 --> 00:06:19.333
are qualities of character,

125
00:06:19.333 --> 00:06:22.125
and abandoning those to chase

126
00:06:22.125 --> 00:06:24.041
the image of looking wealthy 

127
00:06:24.041 --> 00:06:26.791
gives only confusion and suffering.

128
00:06:26.791 --> 00:06:29.958
But the moment you drop the mask and accept

129
00:06:29.958 --> 00:06:32.291
your own self –

130
00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:33.958
‘Yes,

131
00:06:33.958 --> 00:06:36.083
I stand here today

132
00:06:36.083 --> 00:06:38.750
and I need to move forward’ –

133
00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:43.125
that is where real transformation begins.

134
00:06:43.125 --> 00:06:46.583
I do not expect perfection from you.

135
00:06:46.583 --> 00:06:49.458
I only want honesty.

136
00:06:49.458 --> 00:06:52.416
Be true to yourself.

137
00:06:52.416 --> 00:06:54.041
Accept your struggles

138
00:06:54.041 --> 00:06:56.583
without shame.

139
00:06:56.583 --> 00:07:00.500
When you walk with truth rather than pretence,

140
00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:03.666
then I walk with you,

141
00:07:03.666 --> 00:07:08.250
and we both move forward together.

142
00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:09.250
Blessings.

143
00:07:13.916 --> 00:07:18.541
In life, words carry great importance.

144
00:07:18.541 --> 00:07:22.750
The tone in which you speak to each other

145
00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:26.041
has a very deep effect.

146
00:07:26.041 --> 00:07:30.291
So deep that you cannot even imagine.

147
00:07:30.291 --> 00:07:34.000
Even if you are right, but

148
00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:36.958
if your words are harsh,

149
00:07:36.958 --> 00:07:39.208
the message is lost

150
00:07:39.208 --> 00:07:42.291
and the relationship is wounded.

151
00:07:42.291 --> 00:07:45.291
A sharp voice,

152
00:07:45.291 --> 00:07:49.250
a sarcastic remark, or a sentence

153
00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:53.666
spoken in anger may seem trivial
in the moment, but

154
00:07:53.666 --> 00:07:54.666
over time

155
00:07:54.666 --> 00:07:57.708
it builds walls within the heart.

156
00:07:57.708 --> 00:08:01.708
These wounds are not visible from
outside, but within

157
00:08:01.708 --> 00:08:04.708
they hurt very deeply.

158
00:08:04.708 --> 00:08:05.666
When children

159
00:08:05.666 --> 00:08:09.791
get low marks in some exam, saying to them –

160
00:08:09.791 --> 00:08:14.291
‘With every comfort, you cannot
even do this much.

161
00:08:14.291 --> 00:08:19.625
The neighbour’s children scored
more than you’ –

162
00:08:19.625 --> 00:08:23.833
this comparison deepens the child’s depression.

163
00:08:23.833 --> 00:08:27.708
But your empathy, once again,

164
00:08:27.708 --> 00:08:31.416
reawakens their confidence.

165
00:08:31.416 --> 00:08:34.333
Harshness drives love away

166
00:08:34.333 --> 00:08:37.166
and makes even ordinary conversation

167
00:08:37.166 --> 00:08:39.416
feel unsafe.

168
00:08:39.416 --> 00:08:43.625
I do not expect perfection from you.

169
00:08:43.625 --> 00:08:47.125
I say again, but I want

170
00:08:47.125 --> 00:08:50.666
you to have compassion.

171
00:08:50.666 --> 00:08:54.541
Pause before reacting.

172
00:08:54.541 --> 00:08:59.041
Do not use truth as a weapon.

173
00:08:59.041 --> 00:09:01.500
Say what is necessary,

174
00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:06.083
but with gentleness and care.

175
00:09:06.083 --> 00:09:11.750
When you keep restraint in your words,

176
00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:13.708
then you protect

177
00:09:13.708 --> 00:09:17.750
the peace of your family.

178
00:09:22.583 --> 00:09:24.416
In the work environment,

179
00:09:24.416 --> 00:09:28.083
the desire for respect is natural,

180
00:09:28.083 --> 00:09:31.958
but when it becomes your need

181
00:09:31.958 --> 00:09:33.791
that without receiving respect

182
00:09:33.791 --> 00:09:37.375
you do not consider yourself important,

183
00:09:37.375 --> 00:09:40.375
then this becomes abhimana.

184
00:09:40.375 --> 00:09:42.916
Ego.

185
00:09:42.916 --> 00:09:48.208
This quality keeps the soul in darkness.

186
00:09:48.208 --> 00:09:50.416
In professional life it silently

187
00:09:50.416 --> 00:09:54.000
weakens both the team and the leadership.

188
00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:58.208
When your attention gets fixed on –

189
00:09:58.208 --> 00:10:02.708
‘Was I appreciated enough?’

190
00:10:02.708 --> 00:10:04.458
or ‘Why don’t those people

191
00:10:04.458 --> 00:10:08.083
give me recognition?’ –

192
00:10:08.083 --> 00:10:11.875
you drift away from the actual work.

193
00:10:11.875 --> 00:10:15.041
Ego creates friction.

194
00:10:15.041 --> 00:10:17.375
It stops you from responding to feedback

195
00:10:17.375 --> 00:10:21.666
and makes it hard to accept suggestions.

196
00:10:21.666 --> 00:10:24.416
It makes you overreact to small things and,

197
00:10:24.416 --> 00:10:27.458
when appreciation

198
00:10:27.458 --> 00:10:31.333
is not given, forces you to withdraw.

199
00:10:31.333 --> 00:10:33.708
Slowly trust diminishes,

200
00:10:33.708 --> 00:10:35.291
because people

201
00:10:35.291 --> 00:10:39.666
walk very carefully around you.

202
00:10:39.666 --> 00:10:41.583
True leadership

203
00:10:41.583 --> 00:10:44.250
is built through contribution,

204
00:10:44.250 --> 00:10:46.791
not titles and praise.

205
00:10:46.791 --> 00:10:50.000
As soon as you let go of this constant

206
00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:53.166
thirst for recognition,

207
00:10:53.166 --> 00:10:55.541
you become more at ease, more

208
00:10:55.541 --> 00:10:58.875
respected, and more effective.

209
00:10:58.875 --> 00:11:00.791
Do not let ego

210
00:11:00.791 --> 00:11:04.666
narrow your vision.

211
00:11:04.666 --> 00:11:06.791
Stay grounded.

212
00:11:06.791 --> 00:11:10.375
Serve with clarity.

213
00:11:10.375 --> 00:11:12.458
Do your best work

214
00:11:12.458 --> 00:11:16.333
and let respect come naturally.

215
00:11:16.333 --> 00:11:19.833
You will not need to ask for this respect.

216
00:11:19.833 --> 00:11:22.541
Your work

217
00:11:22.541 --> 00:11:24.166
will speak it.

218
00:11:24.166 --> 00:11:30.625
Remember, true respect is earned,

219
00:11:30.625 --> 00:11:31.916
not demanded.
